 November 13.","t_yest":"November 13: a typical high, but a warm night","p_yest":"The high of <strong>51\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 55\u00b0F, and the record is 80\u00b0F (2007). The low of <strong>35\u00b0F</strong> was the 7th warmest November 13 low (tied) of 120 since 1895.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Goodland's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Goodland has set <strong>52 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 83 that chance alone would give, and <strong>121 record highs</strong>, more than the 83 that chance alone would give. The 1930s hold the most record highs of any decade (65). Goodland's all-time high is 111\u00b0F, on July 25, 1940.","t_chg":"Goodland's nights show no clear change. Its days have warmed since 1986.","p_chg":"Across 110 complete years: Goodland's average low shows no clear change: +0.05\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.03 to +0.14) that includes zero. Goodland's average high shows no clear change: +0.06\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.07 to +0.18) that includes zero. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows show no clear change and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.74\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.28 to +1.20). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 3 of 12 months. Highs rose in 1 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Goodland's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.20 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 19.1 inches a year. The wettest year was 1923 (28.20 in); the driest, 1956 (9.19 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 8 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}